{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The threshold showing is made out on this trip and nowhere else. trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip identifier TRP-00111 and agree on the pickup/start at 2026-08-03T07:47:40+08:00, so POL-RD-08(a) is satisfied; and on the trace figure that governs under POL-RD-01 (trace_distance_km 29.98, not the rounded actual_distance_km 30.0) the excess over the booked optimal of 24.0 km is 5.98 km and 24.92% — past both the 0.8 km and the 20% gates. The burden therefore shifts to the driver under POL-RD-08, and the driver discharges it the way that clause requires: by pointing to a specific artifact and a specific clause, not by a general assertion that traffic was bad.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00111", "EV-GPS-00111", "EV-FARE-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The excess is exonerated outright under POL-RD-03. The artefact is EV-ADVIS-00111-01, an LTA DataMall CLOSURE on the 'Pan Island Expressway (PIE) towards Tuas, after Clementi Rd exit' — a segment the booked optimal route uses (the trip record's optimal_route_source is 'BKE southbound then PIE westbound'), so limb (a) is met. Its validity window is 07:10–09:30, bracketing the 07:47:40–08:25:40 trip by far more than the 15-minute buffer limb (b) allows, with 41.5 minutes of overlap and overlaps_trip_window true. The 10-second, 100%-coverage trace on EV-GPS-00111 shows the vehicle leaving the optimal corridor at Bukit Panjang before the closed segment and rejoining it on the AYE, which is limb (c). All three conditions are satisfied.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00111-01", "EV-GPS-00111", "EV-TRIP-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.intersects_route",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The exoneration is not merely partial — it covers the whole measured excess. The POL-RD-03 cap is 1.30 x the ADDITIONAL distance of the shortest lawful alternative over the booked optimal, plus 1.0 km of tolerance: 1.30 x (29.2 - 24.0) + 1.00 = 7.76 km. The measured excess is 5.98 km, which is less than 7.76 km, so justified_excess_km is the measured figure itself and there is no unexonerated residue left for POL-RD-02 to operate on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00111", "EV-ADVIS-00111-01", "EV-GPS-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.cap_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The routing is the authority's own diversion, not a discretionary shortcut: the advisory text on EV-ADVIS-00111-01 reads 'Diversion via Upper Bukit Timah Rd', which is exactly the road the rider's own claim text describes the driver using ('came off at Bukit Panjang and went down Upper Bukit Timah and around by the AYE'). The driver took the published way round a HIGH-severity closure of the corridor the optimal route uses.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00111-01", "EV-TRIP-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Run POL-RD-02 against the closure-adjusted optimal that POL-RD-03 requires — 24.0 + 5.98 = 29.98 km, duration scaled from the booked 30.0 min to 37.5 min — and the money simply is not there: recomputed_fare = 3.80 + 0.75 x 29.98 + 0.28 x 37.5 + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP = 37.585, against a charged_total of 37.74. The difference is SGD 0.155, below the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so under POL-RD-02 read with POL-RD-03 the outcome is NO_ACTION and the charged fare of SGD 37.74 stands as recorded on EV-FARE-00111 (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00111", "EV-TRIP-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no pass-through correction to add on top. EV-FARE-00111 records tolls_erp 0.00 and an empty erp_gantries list, and the trace crosses no gantry, so the standalone off-route ERP refund that POL-RD-09 gives even an exonerated closure has nothing to operate on and the SGD 12.00 cap on that head is not reached. The distance and time charges stand because POL-RD-03 places the closure beyond the driver's control, and the rider's own claim that he 'did not see any closure' does not put a gantry on the trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00111", "EV-GPS-00111", "EV-ADVIS-00111-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log confirms the driver told the rider before he diverted — MSG-00111-001, sent 07:54:20, 'boss PIE towards tuas closed, lorry fire. i come off at bukit panjang ok' — and the rider read it and answered at 07:54:55, 'as long as i reach by 8.30', without objecting to the route. I do not put this forward as a rider-instructed detour and do not rely on POL-RD-04, because the rider requested no waypoint and waypoint_hint is null; it is offered as contemporaneous notice that corroborates the driver's account of why he left the corridor and rebuts any suggestion the diversion was concealed or self-serving.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00111", "EV-ADVIS-00111-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation scrutiny is engaged. POL-RD-06 is triggered only by a MATERIAL deviation — excess over 50% of optimal or over 8.0 km absolute, on the excess REMAINING after adjustment — and after the POL-RD-03 cap is applied there is no remaining excess at all, while the raw figures (24.92%, 5.98 km) sit below both materiality thresholds. Were the profile consulted, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 588, which establishes no pattern on the test POL-RD-06 actually states.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00111", "EV-GPS-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.thresholds.material_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the fare of SGD 37.74 stands, and no refund is due. This is not a driver taking a route of his own choosing — the record shows he followed a published road closure diversion.\n\nEV-ADVIS-00111-01 is an LTA DataMall closure on the Pan Island Expressway towards Tuas, the corridor the platform's optimal route (BKE southbound then PIE westbound) uses: a HIGH-severity vehicle fire, all lanes closed between Clementi Rd and Jalan Anak Bukit, valid 07:10–09:30 — which brackets the 07:47:40–08:25:40 trip with far more than the 15-minute buffer — overlapping 41.5 minutes, intersecting the route, and diverting traffic via Upper Bukit Timah Rd. That is exactly the road the driver used.\n\nPOL-RD-03 is satisfied on all three limbs. (a) The advisory names a segment the optimal route traverses. (b) Its window overlaps the trip. (c) The trace on EV-GPS-00111 — 229 fixes at a steady 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0 — shows the vehicle leaving the optimal corridor at Bukit Panjang, before the closed segment, and rejoining it on the AYE on the final run-in to the booked drop-off at one-north. On the rider's point that the rejoin is on the AYE rather than the PIE: the AYE is the destination-side approach to one-north, and the leave-before / rejoin-after pattern the clause requires is present on the trace; the driver also told the rider in-app at 07:54:20 that the PIE was closed and that he was coming off at Bukit Panjang, and the rider did not object.\n\nThe exoneration is capped, and the cap does not bite: 1.30 × (29.2 − 24.0) + 1.00 = 7.76 km against a measured excess of 5.98 km, so the whole excess is justified and no deviation remains under POL-RD-01. Running POL-RD-02 against the closure-adjusted optimal route (29.98 km, 37.5 min) gives a recomputed fare of SGD 37.585 against SGD 37.74 charged — SGD 0.155, below the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so nothing issues. The SGD 6.75 figure the rider's advocate computes is the booked-route calculation, and it does not apply once the closure is accounted for.\n\nThe trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (no gap over 90 s, no jump over 500 m, no sampling interval above 30 s), so no escalation arises on that head. POL-RD-04 is not engaged — no rider instructed the detour, waypoint_hint is null on both chat messages, and the driver's exoneration rests on POL-RD-03 alone; the chat log is contemporaneous notice, not a detour request. POL-RD-09 has nothing to settle: tolls_erp is 0.00, erp_gantries is empty, neither route crosses a gantry at this hour, and there is no unmatched charge line and so no billing-integrity defect. POL-RD-06 is not engaged: this is not a material deviation, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 588 completed trips, so there is no pattern and no conduct referral. The rider's statement that he saw no closure is a bare assertion and does not outweigh the transport authority's own advisory. The party profiles were used only as context in accordance with POL-GEN-01."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
